;; fault-reserved.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-reserved.s` (P2-SCALAR.3).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py fault-reserved.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "fault-reserved.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-reserved.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). The reserved case keeps its source meaning (SEM-07): the model reports the UNSPECIFIED" "case as such (Stop::Undefined), and the laboratory's declared D-RESERVED-DECODE policy — the" "harness's explicit act — converts it to the illegal-instruction observation. Both references raise" "illegal-instruction with tval = the offending word (measured), so the converted observation is" "three-way comparable.")
(expectations (program "fault-reserved.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (step (n 0) (insn "addi x1, x0, 1") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000000001"))) (derivation "An ordinary write, so the reserved word is not the only step.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 1) (insn ".word 0xFFFFFFFF") (writes) (derivation "0xFFFFFFFF matches no row of the generated decode table: a RESERVED instruction, whose behavior the architecture declares UNSPECIFIED. This laboratory's policy (D-RESERVED-DECODE) raises illegal-instruction, with tval = the offending word — measured on both references as cause 0x02, tval 0x00000000FFFFFFFF. The step writes no register.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5.2 (the reserved-instruction note: UNSPECIFIED) — decision D-RESERVED-DECODE (the laboratory policy over the UNSPECIFIED case)")))
